# shell: desktop
# setup: bandscroll
# PVL-046: rows arriving ABOVE what is on screen must not push the listing
# down under the reader.  The view records how far it was pushed; nothing
# applied it, so a folder that gains files while you read the middle of it
# scrolls away from you.
wait 8
note walked down the listing, so there are rows above the viewport and
note room below it -- at the very bottom the clamp would hide an overshoot
key Home
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
key Down
wait 8
expect-scroll 5
expect-scroll-at-most 5
note two files arrive that sort above everything on screen
write /tmp/trk_script/aaa1.txt x
write /tmp/trk_script/aaa2.txt x
wait 60
note the reader is still looking at the same rows: two arrived above, so
note the offset moved by two and the window did not
expect-scroll 7
expect-scroll-at-most 7
note and the window as a whole is what a full redraw would draw
expect-same-as-redraw
quit
